       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum acetaminophen dose for an adult of 4,000 mg/day. Even with normal liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of hepatotoxicity. Many institutions also cap it lower, at 3 g/day, for some patients.\n\nHere are some ways I could enter it:\n- **3000 mg/day total:** 1000 mg PO three times daily.\n- **4000 mg/day total:** 1000 mg PO four times daily. A dose of 650 mg every 4\u20136 hours is another standard option, as long as the total stays under the cap.\n- **Something else:** If you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. For example, 3000 mg might have been meant as the daily total, not the per-dose amount.\n\nIf 3000 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm. I'd also want to know the clinical reason, so the order can be documented properly."
      }
