      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range that can cause acute liver injury or liver failure. I don't know of any clinical situation where a scheduled dose that high is appropriate, and you haven't given a reason for it. I'd rather not put it into the system, where it could be given as written.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within safe limits.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or four times daily (4 g/day). I can enter either one now.\n- **Add a note** if you need more analgesia than that. Options include a multimodal regimen with an NSAID if appropriate, or a short opioid course.\n- **Involve pharmacy.** If you think this dose is intended, the clinical pharmacist or your attending should review it first. Most order systems would flag it for hard-stop verification.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
